{
  "id": "21334_yusen",
  "headword": "{湯煎|ゆせん}",
  "reading": "ゆせん",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "water bath; double boiling; bain-marie",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "water bath; double boiling; bain-marie",
      "explanation": "A cooking technique where food is heated indirectly by placing its container in a larger pot of hot water. Used for gentle, even heating — common for melting chocolate, heating retort pouches, and making delicate sauces."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21334_yusen_ex1",
      "japanese": "チョコレートを{湯煎|ゆせん}で{溶|と}かす。",
      "english": "To melt chocolate in a water bath.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21334_yusen_ex2",
      "japanese": "レトルトカレーを{湯煎|ゆせん}で{温|あたた}めた。",
      "english": "I heated the retort curry in a water bath.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21334_yusen_ex3",
      "japanese": "バターは{直火|じかび}ではなく{湯煎|ゆせん}でゆっくり{溶|と}かした{方|ほう}がいい。",
      "english": "It's better to melt butter slowly in a water bath rather than over direct heat.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {湯|ゆ} (hot water) + {煎|せん} (roast, boil). A fundamental cooking technique found on food packaging instructions and in recipes throughout Japan. Retort food packages commonly instruct users to heat by {湯煎|ゆせん}.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {湯煎|ゆせん}で{溶|と}かす: to melt in a water bath\n- {湯煎|ゆせん}で{温|あたた}める: to warm in a water bath\n- {湯煎|ゆせん}にかける: to put in a water bath\n- {湯煎|ゆせん}{可能|かのう}: can be heated by water bath (packaging label)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {直火|じかび}: direct heat (cooking directly over flame)\n- {蒸|む}す: to steam (using steam to cook, different from water bath)\n- {電子|でんし}レンジ: microwave (modern alternative for reheating)",
